WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.145
<v Examiner>Four marks.

2
00:00:02.145 --> 00:00:04.750
<v Examiner>Describe the four levels of prevention.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:10.562
<v Examiner>Link each one to upstream, midstream or downstream, and give a nursing example of each.

4
00:00:11.012 --> 00:00:14.863
Lisa's memory hooks are on her slides: primary, prevent.

5
00:00:14.863 --> 00:00:16.100
Secondary, screen.

6
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:17.200
Tertiary, treat.

7
00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.951
And primordial comes before all of them.

8
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:24.922
Primordial prevention stops the risk factors themselves from developing.

9
00:00:24.922 --> 00:00:28.313
It works on the social determinants, so it's upstream.

10
00:00:28.313 --> 00:00:32.395
Her example: a nurse advocating for better housing and transport,

11
00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:34.468
like the Healthy Homes standards.

12
00:00:34.468 --> 00:00:39.366
A warm, dry house prevents respiratory illness and stops asthma getting worse.

13
00:00:39.816 --> 00:00:45.447
Primary prevention prevents disease once risk factors exist, before it ever starts.

14
00:00:45.447 --> 00:00:50.195
It's aimed at populations and high-risk groups, upstream to midstream.

15
00:00:50.195 --> 00:00:56.029
Examples: the vaccination schedule, health education, and workplace safety like P P E.

16
00:00:56.479 --> 00:01:01.815
Secondary prevention is screening: detecting disease early to stop it progressing.

17
00:01:01.815 --> 00:01:02.921
That's midstream.

18
00:01:02.921 --> 00:01:08.191
Examples: cervical screening, mammograms, bowel screening, and regular check-ups.

19
00:01:08.641 --> 00:01:12.389
Tertiary prevention manages a disease that already exists,

20
00:01:12.389 --> 00:01:15.555
to stop it getting worse and to limit disability.

21
00:01:15.555 --> 00:01:16.718
That's downstream.

22
00:01:16.718 --> 00:01:20.659
Her example: helping someone manage diabetes after diagnosis.

23
00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:25.634
The right medicines, knowing what they're for, taking them, follow-up bloods.

24
00:01:25.634 --> 00:01:28.993
All of that prevents kidney and heart complications.

25
00:01:29.443 --> 00:01:34.881
And the point she made about both frameworks: a nurse has to work at every level at once,

26
00:01:34.881 --> 00:01:35.676
not just one.

27
00:01:35.676 --> 00:01:37.631
Upstream changes the conditions.

28
00:01:37.631 --> 00:01:40.686
Downstream looks after the person in front of you.

29
00:01:41.136 --> 00:01:46.158
Primordial: stop risk factors developing, the social determinants, upstream,

30
00:01:46.158 --> 00:01:47.413
like Healthy Homes.

31
00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:51.840
Primary, prevent: vaccination and education, upstream to midstream.

32
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:56.003
Secondary, screen: early detection, midstream, like mammograms.

33
00:01:56.003 --> 00:02:01.025
Tertiary, treat: manage existing disease, downstream, like diabetes support.

34
00:02:01.025 --> 00:02:02.875
Work at every level at once.
